1
00:00:01,575 --> 00:00:03,635
Last time, we counted legs.

2
00:00:03,905 --> 00:00:05,285
Insects have six.

3
00:00:05,555 --> 00:00:08,665
And we met the reptiles, with dry, scaly skin.

4
00:00:08,945 --> 00:00:10,055
Like Basil!

5
00:00:10,108 --> 00:00:11,628
Cold-blooded, and proud!

6
00:00:13,443 --> 00:00:14,773
Today you'll learn...

7
00:00:14,940 --> 00:00:16,460
How to spot a mammal.

8
00:00:16,627 --> 00:00:18,347
Which one does not belong.

9
00:00:18,515 --> 00:00:20,665
Same and different, with a reason.

10
00:00:21,470 --> 00:00:22,700
Lock in first.

11
00:00:22,970 --> 00:00:25,380
A little squirrel is hiding in this video.

12
00:00:25,670 --> 00:00:26,870
Can you spot it?

13
00:00:30,196 --> 00:00:31,076
Round one.

14
00:00:31,376 --> 00:00:32,986
This animal has wings.

15
00:00:33,266 --> 00:00:34,266
It flies.

16
00:00:34,546 --> 00:00:35,756
Is a bat a bird?

17
00:00:36,076 --> 00:00:37,156
One, yes.

18
00:00:37,426 --> 00:00:38,286
Two, no.

19
00:00:38,576 --> 00:00:40,056
Show me with your fingers.

20
00:00:45,522 --> 00:00:46,502
Locked in!

21
00:00:46,630 --> 00:00:47,250
One!

22
00:00:47,390 --> 00:00:48,840
It flies, like a bird!

23
00:00:48,891 --> 00:00:49,651
Two!

24
00:00:49,741 --> 00:00:51,301
I think I see fur.

25
00:00:51,347 --> 00:00:52,137
Two.

26
00:00:52,407 --> 00:00:53,627
No feathers.

27
00:00:54,049 --> 00:00:54,929
Be a hair!

28
00:00:55,219 --> 00:00:56,199
Shrink down.

29
00:00:56,479 --> 00:00:57,409
Quietly.

30
00:00:59,700 --> 00:01:01,887
You are one hair on a fruit bat's back.

31
00:01:02,370 --> 00:01:05,154
Soft fur, like a forest, all around you.

32
00:01:05,719 --> 00:01:07,179
It spreads its wings.

33
00:01:07,629 --> 00:01:08,639
Thin skin.

34
00:01:09,079 --> 00:01:10,229
No feathers!

35
00:01:10,817 --> 00:01:11,647
Whoosh!

36
00:01:12,127 --> 00:01:13,407
Out into the night.

37
00:01:13,827 --> 00:01:15,057
The air is cool.

38
00:01:15,467 --> 00:01:17,477
But the body under you stays warm.

39
00:01:18,129 --> 00:01:21,699
Back at the palm, a baby bat drinks its mother's milk.

40
00:01:24,121 --> 00:01:25,431
The answer is two.

41
00:01:25,711 --> 00:01:27,191
A bat is not a bird.

42
00:01:27,481 --> 00:01:28,681
It is a mammal!

43
00:01:31,542 --> 00:01:32,572
Two fingers?

44
00:01:32,842 --> 00:01:34,062
One finger up!

45
00:01:34,110 --> 00:01:34,740
Fur!

46
00:01:34,910 --> 00:01:36,020
Not feathers!

47
00:01:36,442 --> 00:01:37,662
Say it with me!

48
00:01:38,375 --> 00:01:42,225
Mammals are animals that have hair or fur as their outer covering.

49
00:01:44,847 --> 00:01:46,947
Monkeys, cats, bats, and you!

50
00:01:47,217 --> 00:01:48,767
They all have hair or fur.

51
00:01:48,820 --> 00:01:50,360
Pip and I are mammals!

52
00:01:50,369 --> 00:01:51,639
And I'm the reptile.

53
00:01:51,759 --> 00:01:53,039
No fur for me!

54
00:01:53,385 --> 00:01:55,955
Most mammals give birth to their young alive.

55
00:01:56,235 --> 00:02:00,655
The females have mammary glands that can produce milk for their young.

56
00:02:03,871 --> 00:02:09,321
Mammals are warm-blooded, which means that they can maintain a constant body

57
00:02:09,071 --> 00:02:10,011
temperature.

58
00:02:14,135 --> 00:02:15,215
Exam tip!

59
00:02:15,505 --> 00:02:17,125
Compare a bat and a bird.

60
00:02:17,249 --> 00:02:20,489
A bat and a bird are similar because both have wings.

61
00:02:20,759 --> 00:02:23,909
They are different because a bat has fur, but a bird has

62
00:02:23,659 --> 00:02:24,429
feathers.

63
00:02:25,948 --> 00:02:26,958
Round two.

64
00:02:27,238 --> 00:02:28,758
Which one does not belong?

65
00:02:29,058 --> 00:02:30,178
One, a cat.

66
00:02:30,458 --> 00:02:31,638
Two, a monkey.

67
00:02:31,908 --> 00:02:33,208
Three, a lizard.

68
00:02:33,498 --> 00:02:34,978
Show me with your fingers.

69
00:02:40,448 --> 00:02:41,428
Locked in!

70
00:02:41,556 --> 00:02:42,446
Two.

71
00:02:42,576 --> 00:02:43,696
The monkey.

72
00:02:43,826 --> 00:02:45,276
It climbs trees.

73
00:02:45,325 --> 00:02:46,025
Three!

74
00:02:46,345 --> 00:02:47,375
No fur.

75
00:02:47,428 --> 00:02:48,128
Three!

76
00:02:48,258 --> 00:02:49,278
Like me!

77
00:02:49,475 --> 00:02:50,835
The answer is three.

78
00:02:51,125 --> 00:02:52,615
Find what the others share.

79
00:02:52,905 --> 00:02:55,575
A cat and a monkey have fur: mammals.

80
00:02:55,855 --> 00:02:59,085
A lizard has dry, scaly skin: a reptile.

81
00:02:59,135 --> 00:03:00,225
Three fingers?

82
00:03:00,495 --> 00:03:01,705
One finger up!

83
00:03:01,755 --> 00:03:02,395
Oops.

84
00:03:02,775 --> 00:03:04,215
Cats climb too!

85
00:03:04,224 --> 00:03:05,424
Scales, not fur.

86
00:03:05,564 --> 00:03:07,034
The odd one out is me!

87
00:03:08,533 --> 00:03:09,163
One.

88
00:03:08,913 --> 00:03:10,783
It has scaly skin.

89
00:03:10,923 --> 00:03:11,533
Two.

90
00:03:11,763 --> 00:03:13,593
It breathes air with its lungs.

91
00:03:13,643 --> 00:03:14,243
Three.

92
00:03:14,603 --> 00:03:16,893
It swims in the sea, so it is a fish!

93
00:03:17,170 --> 00:03:18,070
Showdown!

94
00:03:18,380 --> 00:03:19,510
Double points.

95
00:03:19,780 --> 00:03:21,400
One line has a mistake.

96
00:03:21,690 --> 00:03:23,450
Line one, two, or three?

97
00:03:23,750 --> 00:03:25,220
Show me with your fingers.

98
00:03:31,695 --> 00:03:32,675
Locked in!

99
00:03:32,803 --> 00:03:33,263
Three.

100
00:03:33,873 --> 00:03:36,063
Fish usually breathe through gills.

101
00:03:36,114 --> 00:03:36,884
Three!

102
00:03:36,914 --> 00:03:38,144
That's my group!

103
00:03:38,199 --> 00:03:38,809
Oops!

104
00:03:39,680 --> 00:03:41,030
Read all the clues.

105
00:03:41,310 --> 00:03:43,870
Scaly skin and lungs: a reptile.

106
00:03:44,230 --> 00:03:45,520
It is a sea turtle!

107
00:03:45,651 --> 00:03:47,011
Showed three fingers?

108
00:03:47,291 --> 00:03:49,191
Put up two more on your score hand!

109
00:03:49,243 --> 00:03:49,923
Fixed!

110
00:03:50,529 --> 00:03:52,059
Six animal groups!

111
00:03:52,854 --> 00:03:53,955
Say it with us!

112
00:03:54,615 --> 00:03:55,525
Six legs?

113
00:03:55,495 --> 00:03:56,365
Insect!

114
00:03:58,215 --> 00:03:59,285
Dry, scaly skin?

115
00:03:59,095 --> 00:04:00,045
Reptile!

116
00:04:01,815 --> 00:04:02,725
Hair or fur?

117
00:04:02,695 --> 00:04:03,531
Mammal!

118
00:04:06,020 --> 00:04:07,170
Exam corner!

119
00:04:07,443 --> 00:04:08,743
Say it with me!

120
00:04:09,454 --> 00:04:13,874
Living things such as plants and animals can be classified based on

121
00:04:13,624 --> 00:04:15,934
common observable characteristics.

122
00:04:16,014 --> 00:04:18,544
There are different types of plants and animals.

123
00:04:21,171 --> 00:04:22,641
Show me your score hand!

124
00:04:22,921 --> 00:04:23,951
More than two?

125
00:04:24,231 --> 00:04:25,611
You beat the Buddies.

126
00:04:25,881 --> 00:04:26,991
Four fingers?

127
00:04:27,261 --> 00:04:28,271
High five!

128
00:04:28,776 --> 00:04:30,166
Did you spot the squirrel?

129
00:04:30,446 --> 00:04:31,926
It was on the palm trunk!

130
00:04:32,196 --> 00:04:34,616
Is it cold-blooded, or warm-blooded?

131
00:04:34,916 --> 00:04:36,216
Tell someone at home.

132
00:04:37,098 --> 00:04:39,388
Next time: fungi and bacteria!

133
00:04:39,678 --> 00:04:40,888
Mould on bread.

134
00:04:41,188 --> 00:04:42,908
Yeast, for making bread.

135
00:04:43,178 --> 00:04:44,438
Both are fungi!

136
00:04:44,718 --> 00:04:46,128
Which one is useful?

137
00:04:46,398 --> 00:04:47,718
Lock in your answer!

138
00:04:48,440 --> 00:04:50,640
Let's read today's key words together!

139
00:04:50,930 --> 00:04:51,690
Ready?

140
00:04:52,027 --> 00:04:52,754
Mammals.

141
00:04:54,240 --> 00:04:55,500
Mammary glands.

142
00:04:57,176 --> 00:04:58,206
Warm-blooded.

143
00:04:59,748 --> 00:05:00,688
Well done!

144
00:05:01,670 --> 00:05:02,774
Say it with us!

145
00:05:03,575 --> 00:05:04,325
Ready?

146
00:05:04,448 --> 00:05:05,108
One!

147
00:05:05,448 --> 00:05:06,148
two!

148
00:05:06,453 --> 00:05:07,628
Now you know!
